{:name "ruby"
 :description "Quality toolset for Ruby / Rails projects — Minitest, Rails-omakase flavored."
 :purposes
 {:test
  {:command "bin/rails test"
   :notes "Full unit suite; green before any handoff. Test stack: Minitest as Rails ships it — plain assertions, fixtures over factories, real objects against the real test database. Doubles only at true external edges (network, clock); Mocha when unavoidable. Do not use RSpec or factory_bot in new tests. rubocop-minitest + rubocop-rails-omakase clean. Plain-Ruby gems (no Rails): bundle exec rake test. Browser/system tests belong under acceptance, never here."}

  :coverage
  {:command "COVERAGE=1 bin/rails test"
   :notes "SimpleCov + simplecov-lcov (enabled in test_helper when COVERAGE is set) writes lcov to coverage/lcov.info. Regenerate before reading any coverage-derived metric; stale coverage invalidates everything built on it."}

  :mutation
  {:command "bundle exec mutant run --integration minitest"
   :install "add mutant-minitest to the Gemfile (free for public opensource; commercial/private use needs a subscription — resolve before making this a bar)"
   :notes "Scope runs to the slice's subjects (e.g. -- 'Bujo::Sync*'). mutant-minitest maps tests to subjects via a cover declaration in each test class — a new test without `cover` is invisible to mutation. Surviving mutants in the slice's scope are work: kill them with better tests or record precisely why each survivor is unkillable."}

  :crap
  {:command "crap4rb --lcov coverage/lcov.info <source-dir>"
   :install "clone github.com/bandoyer/crap4rb and symlink exe/crap4rb onto PATH (e.g. into ~/.local/bin)"
   :notes "CRAP = complexity^2 x (1-coverage)^3 + complexity, computed per method from source + lcov — same formula and bar as crap4net: every method <= 6 (exit 2 lists offenders). Requires fresh coverage first."}

  :dry
  {:command "jscpd --min-tokens 50 --reporters console <source-dir>"
   :install "npm install -g jscpd"
   :notes "Language-agnostic; same tool and bar as the dotnet toolset. Duplication within the slice's scope gets removed or explicitly justified."}

  :boundaries
  {:command "bin/packwerk check"
   :install "add packwerk to the Gemfile, then bin/rails g packwerk:install"
   :notes "Packwerk enforces package boundaries; start as one root package and carve out a package only when a boundary is worth defending. Plain-Ruby gems: a dedicated Minitest boundary test asserting the require graph instead."}

  :acceptance
  {:command "bin/rails test:system"
   :notes "Rails system tests (Capybara + headless browser) are the acceptance layer — the omakase answer, no Gherkin runner. Slow by design: never fold into the unit lane, and mutation never runs against it."}}

 :doctor
 [["ruby" "--version"]
  ["bundle" "--version"]
  ["jscpd" "--version"]
  ["crap4rb" "--help"]]}
